# Build config fragment appended to build.config.gki.aarch64 via
# --gki_build_config_fragment. kernel_build_config cat's its srcs in order and
# this fragment is last (common_kernels.bzl), and build.config.gki.aarch64
# sources GKI_BUILD_CONFIG_FRAGMENT after build.config.gki has already run, so
# assignments here win.
#
# build.config.gki sets POST_DEFCONFIG_CMDS="check_defconfig", and
# check_defconfig (build/kernel/_setup_env.sh) runs `savedefconfig` and diffs
# the result against the whole arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig, failing the
# build on any mismatch. This pipeline appends KSU, SUSFS, BBR, NTSync,
# NetHunter and debloat options to that file, so the diff can never be empty.
#
# Clearing it keeps the appends authoritative. Individual options are still
# verified: options that must take effect are asserted after the build by the
# "Verify Bazel defconfig" step, which greps the resolved .config.
POST_DEFCONFIG_CMDS=""
